    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115097" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῠμ-εία</span></b> , ἡ, the
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>art of alloying metals,
				alchemy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Zos.Alch.
			</span></i> ap. Syncell.<i><span class="en">
				p.24
			</span></i> Dindorf (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημεία,</span>
			but <i>khumia</i> in the Syriac version, Diels <i>Antike Technik</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				p.109
			</span></i>), Olymp.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.94
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμεία</span>), Joann.<i><span class="en">
				Antioch.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				15.3
			</span></i> (<u>FHG</u>iv<i><span class="en">
				p.548
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημ-</span>), and so <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέρας</span>
			, but (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειμ-</span>) in <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>Incred.</u>
				3
			</span></i> cod.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				165
			</span></i> (<u>FHG</u>iv<i><span class="en">
				p.601
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημία</span> cod.P, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημεία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Suid.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διοκλητιανός</span>
			 (vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειμεία, μοιχεία</span>),
			Id. 
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημεία</span>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειμ-</span>
			)). (Named from its supposed inventor <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χύμης</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημ- χειμ-</span>
			) acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Zos.Alch.
			</span></i> l.c., cf. eund.<i><span class="en">
				pp.169,172
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμ-</span>), Olymp.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.84B.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χημ-</span>); more prob. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χύμα,</span> cf. Diels l.c.)</div>
